    "body": "> † Categories in the \"Parents\" column refer to parents that list the given categories in their content model, **not to elements that themselves are in those categories**. For example, the a element's \"Parents\" column says \"phrasing\", so any element whose content model contains the \"phrasing\" category could be a parent of an a element. Since the \"flow\" category includes all the \"phrasing\" elements, that means the th element could be a parent to an a element.\n",
